Rem ==================================================================
Rem thornle-core.shoddy — Thornle, the pure model.
Rem
Rem Everything the game IS that does not touch a terminal: the word
Rem list as the game uses it, the scoring of a guess against the answer,
Rem the state record, the line classifier and the keyboard legend. No
Rem Print, no Input, no file read and no cursor addressing, so it runs
Rem headless and is checked that way by test.shoddy. thornle.shoddy adds
Rem the VT100 painting, the menu and the loop on top.
Rem
Rem The decisions the rest depends on:
Rem   - The shell reads the file; the core takes a List Of String and
Rem     never knows where it came from. That is what lets the tests hand
Rem     it ten words.
Rem   - Input is a whole line, not a key. Classify turns one line into
Rem     an Action; the terminal does the editing.
Rem   - Marks are not stored. The shell recomputes them from the answer
Rem     and each guess when it paints, because scoring five letters is
Rem     cheaper than keeping two lists in step.
Rem   - Scoring handles repeated letters the way the original game does:
Rem     exact hits first, each consuming its answer letter; then, left to
Rem     right, a remaining guess letter is wrong-place if an unconsumed
Rem     copy is left (and consumes it), otherwise absent.
Rem ==================================================================

Include "seq.shoddy"
Include "str.shoddy"
Include "math.shoddy"

Rem ---- tunables ------------------------------------------------------

Let wordLen = 5
Let maxGuesses = 6

Rem ---- the word list -------------------------------------------------

Rem A playable word: exactly five letters a-z.
Def IsWord(s As String) As Boolean
    Len(s) = wordLen And All(Codes(s), Fn(c) => c >= 97 And c <= 122)

Rem The list as the game uses it: lowercased, trimmed, and only the
Rem five-letter words kept. The shipped file is already clean, so this
Rem costs nothing and protects the game from a list somebody edits.
Def Normalise(lines As List Of String) As List Of String
    Filter(Map(lines, Fn(s) => Lower(Trim(s))), IsWord)

Rem ---- marks ---------------------------------------------------------

Rem Right letter in the right place; right letter in the wrong place;
Rem letter not in the word.
Type Mark = Placed | Present | Absent

Rem The second pass's working state: the marks so far, and how many
Rem unconsumed copies of each letter the answer still has.
Type Scoring
    ScMarks As Array Of Mark
    ScSpare As Array Of Number

Rem a = 1 .. z = 26
Def LetterIx(code As Number) As Number
    code - 96

Def Hit(ans As String, gs As String, i As Number) As Boolean
    CodeAt(ans, i) = CodeAt(gs, i)

Def Bump(counts As Array Of Number, k As Number, d As Number) As Array Of Number
    SetNth(counts, k, Nth(counts, k) + d)

Rem Pass one: the answer's letters at the positions that are not exact
Rem hits, counted per letter.
Def SpareCounts(ans As String, gs As String) As Array Of Number
    Fold(Range(1, wordLen), Dim(26, 0), Fn(acc, i) => SpareAdd(acc, ans, gs, i))

Def SpareAdd(acc As Array Of Number, ans As String, gs As String, i As Number) As Array Of Number
    If Hit(ans, gs, i) Then
        acc
    Else
        Bump(acc, LetterIx(CodeAt(ans, i)), 1)

Rem The five marks for a guess against the answer.
Def Marks(ans As String, gs As String) As Array Of Mark
    Let start = Scoring(Dim(wordLen, Absent()), SpareCounts(ans, gs))
    ScMarks(Fold(Range(1, wordLen), start, Fn(sc, i) => MarkAt(sc, ans, gs, i)))

Rem Pass two, one position: an exact hit is Placed; otherwise the guess
Rem letter is Present if a spare copy is left, and consumes it.
Def MarkAt(sc As Scoring, ans As String, gs As String, i As Number) As Scoring
    If Hit(ans, gs, i) Then
        With(sc, ScMarks = SetNth(ScMarks(sc), i, Placed()))
    Else
        MarkSpare(sc, i, LetterIx(CodeAt(gs, i)))

Def MarkSpare(sc As Scoring, i As Number, k As Number) As Scoring
    If Nth(ScSpare(sc), k) > 0 Then
        Scoring(SetNth(ScMarks(sc), i, Present()), Bump(ScSpare(sc), k, -1))
    Else
        sc

Rem ---- the game ------------------------------------------------------

Rem One record, threaded through the loop and replaced, never changed.
Rem Note is the message line: "", or why a line was refused, or how the
Rem game ended.
Type Game
    Answer  As String
    Words   As List Of String
    Guesses As List Of String
    Note    As String
    Won     As Boolean
    Ended   As Boolean

Rem The answer is picked with Pick; the shell seeds first.
Def NewGame(ws As List Of String) As Game
    Game(Pick(ws), ws, { }, "", False, False)

Rem A submitted line. Rejected lines leave the guesses alone and set
Rem the note; once the game has ended nothing changes.
Def Submit(g As Game, t As String) As Game
    If Ended(g) Then
        g
    Else
        If Not IsWord(t) Then
            With(g, Note = "FIVE LETTERS")
        Else
            If Not Contains(Words(g), t) Then
                With(g, Note = "NOT IN THE LIST")
            Else
                Accept(g, t)

Def Accept(g As Game, t As String) As Game
    Let tried = Append(Guesses(g), t)
    Let isWin = t = Answer(g)
    Let isOver = isWin Or Length(tried) >= maxGuesses
    With(g, Guesses = tried, Won = isWin, Ended = isOver, Note = Outcome(isWin, isOver, Length(tried), Answer(g)))

Def Outcome(isWin As Boolean, isOver As Boolean, n As Number, ans As String) As String
    If isWin Then
        "GOT IT IN " & Str(n)
    Else
        If isOver Then
            "IT WAS " & Upper(ans)
        Else
            ""

Rem ---- lines ---------------------------------------------------------

Rem What one typed line means. Q or QUIT alone leaves the game; a blank
Rem line does nothing; anything else is a guess, lowercased and trimmed.
Rem Any five-letter word is a guess, so a word that starts with Q is
Rem never mistaken for quit.
Type Action = Guess(Typed) | Leave | Idle

Def Classify(line As String) As Action
    Let t = Lower(Trim(line))
    If t = "q" Or t = "quit" Then
        Leave()
    Else
        If t = "" Then
            Idle()
        Else
            Guess(t)

Rem Leave is the shell's to act on; the game itself only sees guesses.
Def Act(g As Game, a As Action) As Game
    Select Case a
        Case Guess(t)
            Submit(g, t)
        Case Else
            g

Rem ---- the keyboard legend -------------------------------------------

Rem The best mark seen so far for each of the 26 letters: None for a
Rem letter never guessed, else Some(mark), where right-place beats
Rem wrong-place beats absent.
Def Legend(g As Game) As Array Of Option
    Fold(Guesses(g), Dim(26, None()), Fn(acc, gs) => LegendRow(acc, Answer(g), gs))

Def LegendRow(acc As Array Of Option, ans As String, gs As String) As Array Of Option
    Let ms = Marks(ans, gs)
    Fold(Range(1, wordLen), acc, Fn(a, i) => LegendAt(a, LetterIx(CodeAt(gs, i)), Nth(ms, i)))

Def LegendAt(acc As Array Of Option, k As Number, m As Mark) As Array Of Option
    SetNth(acc, k, Some(Better(Nth(acc, k), m)))

Def Rank(m As Mark) As Number
    Select Case m
        Case Placed
            3
        Case Present
            2
        Case Else
            1

Def Better(old As Option, m As Mark) As Mark
    Select Case old
        Case Some(o)
            Ifte(Rank(o) >= Rank(m), o, m)
        Case None
            m
